{"data":{"id":"10.48550/arxiv.2604.25918","type":"dois","attributes":{"doi":"10.48550/arxiv.2604.25918","prefix":"10.48550","suffix":"arxiv.2604.25918","identifiers":[{"identifier":"2604.25918","identifierType":"arXiv"}],"alternateIdentifiers":[{"alternateIdentifierType":"arXiv","alternateIdentifier":"2604.25918"}],"creators":[{"name":"Zigdon, Yoav","nameType":"Personal","givenName":"Yoav","familyName":"Zigdon","affiliation":[],"nameIdentifiers":[]}],"titles":[{"title":"de Sitter in String Theory vs. Gibbons \u0026amp; Hawking"}],"publisher":"arXiv","container":{},"publicationYear":2026,"subjects":[{"lang":"en","subject":"High Energy Physics - Theory (hep-th)","subjectScheme":"arXiv"},{"subject":"FOS: Physical sciences","subjectScheme":"Fields of Science and Technology (FOS)"}],"contributors":[],"dates":[{"date":"2026-04-28T17:59:59Z","dateType":"Submitted","dateInformation":"v1"},{"date":"2026-04-29T01:07:51Z","dateType":"Updated","dateInformation":"v1"},{"date":"2026-05-03T15:52:22Z","dateType":"Submitted","dateInformation":"v2"},{"date":"2026-05-05T01:05:54Z","dateType":"Updated","dateInformation":"v2"},{"date":"2026-10-09T13:22:34Z","dateType":"Submitted","dateInformation":"v3"},{"date":"2026-10-12T01:02:59Z","dateType":"Updated","dateInformation":"v3"},{"date":"2026-04","dateType":"Available","dateInformation":"v1"}],"language":null,"types":{"ris":"GEN","bibtex":"misc","citeproc":"article","schemaOrg":"CreativeWork","resourceType":"Article","resourceTypeGeneral":"Preprint"},"relatedIdentifiers":[{"relationType":"IsVersionOf","relatedIdentifier":"10.1007/jhep10(2026)081","relatedIdentifierType":"DOI"}],"relatedItems":[],"sizes":[],"formats":[],"version":"3","rightsList":[{"rights":"Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International","rightsUri":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/legalcode","schemeUri":"https://spdx.org/licenses/","rightsIdentifier":"cc-by-4.0","rightsIdentifierScheme":"SPDX"}],"descriptions":[{"description":"This paper corroborates a statement that perturbative string theory does not admit a solution whose spacetime metric is de Sitter times a closed manifold, to all orders in the $α'$ and $g_s$ expansions, under the assumption that the logarithm of the sphere partition function of Euclidean quantum gravity receives a nonzero contribution proportional to $\\frac{1}{G_N}$ in a saddle-point approximation. This assumption is related to the Gibbons-Hawking proposal that the entropy of the cosmological horizon of the static patch is $\\frac{A}{4G_N}$. Evidence for the statement comes from independent approaches to the effective action of string theory, all of which agree that the tree-level action vanishes for closed Euclidean target-space solutions. One possible implication is that the state of the Universe will depart from an asymptotically de Sitter spacetime.","descriptionType":"Abstract"},{"description":"comments are welcome! V2: added a reference and edited slightly to improve wordings. V3: slight edits, text matches a published version at JHEP","descriptionType":"Other"}],"geoLocations":[],"fundingReferences":[],"xml":"","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2604.25918","contentUrl":null,"metadataVersion":2,"schemaVersion":"http://datacite.org/schema/kernel-4","source":"mds","isActive":true,"state":"findable","reason":null,"viewCount":0,"viewsOverTime":[],"downloadCount":0,"downloadsOverTime":[],"referenceCount":0,"citationCount":0,"citationsOverTime":[],"partCount":0,"partOfCount":0,"versionCount":0,"versionOfCount":1,"created":"2026-04-29T02:25:55.000Z","registered":"2026-04-29T02:25:56.000Z","published":"2026","updated":"2026-10-12T02:51:43.000Z"},"relationships":{"client":{"data":{"id":"arxiv.content","type":"clients"}},"provider":{"data":{"id":"arxiv","type":"providers"}},"media":{"data":{"id":"10.48550/arxiv.2604.25918","type":"media"}},"references":{"data":[]},"citations":{"data":[]},"parts":{"data":[]},"partOf":{"data":[]},"versions":{"data":[]},"versionOf":{"data":[{"id":"10.1007/jhep10(2026)081","